{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095213-manufacturing-quality-of-the-m20-pod-book","id":1095213,"title":"Manufacturing quality of the M20 pod book","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-21T13:05:40-07:00","id":1095213,"title":"Manufacturing quality of the M20 pod book","content":"Hi everyone, this is the first post I've made on a web forum in years. I'm trying to start a new Mage game! It'd be my second time ever running a tabletop. I ST'ed a vtm chronicle last year and loved it. I want to run Mage. I picked up the quick start off of eBay and have muddled together a few books with different rules. I want to get the huge M20 book, but on drivethrurpg there are some comments saying the weight and poor binding have caused their copies to fall apart. What are some of y'alls experiences with the book's manufacture, and for that matter with the print on demand onyx books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13433-mr_flood","name":"mr_flood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T14:25:40-07:00","id":1095241,"title":"","content":"Print on Demand is glued to the binding as opposed to more traditional bindings for hard copy, which means that larger texts don't tend to hold up as well (especially if you go for the higher grade paper/color printing). So a 600+ page tome like M20 tends to separate from the binding very rapidly. Smaller books in the &lt;300 page range do just fine in my experience, it's the corebooks for the 20th line that don't hold up well to being passed around the table or treated anything less than delicately. If you want to get more mileage out of it, I would go for the regular quality printing and just give the book a little more care than you might normally for a traditional bound book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12563-inathicon","name":"iNathicon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T10:46:28-07:00","id":1095550,"title":"","content":"I had to get my standard quality copy replaced after only a month of very light use. The cover just slipped off. I was understandably upset and contacted DriveThruRPG. They sent a replacement and it's held up fine. I took the first copy to a local book repair shop and had the binding fixed, so I have multiple functional copies now. Overall I found the customer service experience to be reasonable enough that I still feel comfortable purchasing products on the site.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T07:09:11-07:00","id":1095893,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the input on the book. I will have to weigh my options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13433-mr_flood","name":"mr_flood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}